{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/tests/store_on_vfs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:38:14.921256Z","id":"1301ac856e3699cf3b51fdfc2b83022f18691710dffe26e5364dc72496b67513","body":{"detail":"migration_64_rebuilds_bot_runs_within_its_cost_a_run_on_the_vfs opens a fresh store (every table at MIGRATIONS.len()), runs BOT_RUNS_AT_63 (DROP TABLE bot_runs, a copy of migration 50's table and indexes, migration 63's ALTER, PRAGMA user_version = 63) and opens again. The second open runs every migration after 63 on tables that are already at the latest shape. Shown at d75222028 by appending `\"CREATE TABLE zz_probe (a TEXT);\"` to MIGRATIONS and running `bazel test //crates/clax-worker:store_on_vfs`: the test panics at store_on_vfs.rs:71 with `MigrationFailed { at: 64, detail: \"table zz_probe already exists ...\" }`; the file's other two tests pass. The next migration that adds a table or a column therefore breaks this test, with a message about the store's open and not the fixture. The copy itself matches migrations 50 and 63 today (crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs:1554-1578, :2151) and those are landed, so it cannot drift; it is 28 lines the test does not need. Also: the test takes the largest commit of the whole open as migration 64's, so a later migration that writes more than 64 does would be measured under its name.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":217},"end":{"line":281},"content_hash":"dfc4b3aa43c50f81d23ce6cccece05e83edda44a8455ad832b167d3e1283ed2d"},"suggested_fix":"Make the database at 63 as the_store_repairs_a_database_an_older_build_migrated_on_the_vfs makes one at 23 (store_on_vfs.rs:151): on the VFS connection, execute clax_store::migrations::MIGRATIONS[..63] joined with `;` and then `PRAGMA user_version = 63`, and delete BOT_RUNS_AT_63 and the first open_store. Tried at d75222028 with the zz_probe migration still appended: //crates/clax-worker:store_on_vfs PASSED.","summary":"The migration-64 VFS test fails as soon as a migration 65 exists: it makes its database at 63 by opening a fresh store at the latest version and swapping in a hand copy of bot_runs","tags":["review","claxbot-surfaces","tests","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/tests/store_on_vfs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T03:59:04.963410Z","id":"64802d7f3e740f2d4ce8c40fd7f2d008aba4dd2247162a2186235f3104f18c48","body":{"detail":"migration_64_rebuilds_bot_runs_within_its_cost_a_run_on_the_vfs (crates/clax-worker/tests/store_on_vfs.rs:252) executes clax_store::migrations::MIGRATIONS[..RUN_BINDINGS_MIGRATION - 1] on the VFS connection and then `PRAGMA user_version = 63`, as the_store_repairs_a_database_an_older_build_migrated_on_the_vfs does for 23; BOT_RUNS_AT_63 and the first open_store are deleted. The Rust steps of migrations 1 to 63 (the install's ID, the seeded cost lines) are not run; none writes bot_runs, and the test's comment says so. For the second point of this record (the largest commit of the whole open taken as migration 64's): MemPages no longer keeps the largest commit; it reads the schema version from the SQLite header in chunk 0 (bytes 60 to 63) before and after each commit and records every commit that changed it (MemPages::steps, store_on_vfs.rs:26). The test takes the one commit that left 64 and fails, listing the open's (version, chunks) steps, when there is not exactly one. Evidence, each with the mutation then reverted: with `\"CREATE TABLE zz_probe (a TEXT);\"` appended to MIGRATIONS, `bazelisk test --lockfile_mode=error --test_env=CLAX_FAKE_EXE_DIR=... --sandbox_writable_path=... //crates/clax-worker:store_on_vfs` printed `//crates/clax-worker:store_on_vfs PASSED in 0.3s`; with `\"CREATE TABLE zz_probe AS SELECT id, hex(randomblob(1000)) AS a FROM bot_runs;\"` appended instead (a migration 65 whose commit is larger than migration 64's for the test's 4,000 runs), the same command printed `PASSED in 0.4s`, so the bound of CHUNKS_PER_THOUSAND_RUNS was applied to migration 64's commit and not to the larger one. The close is left to the owner: this branch's commits are unsigned and their SHAs will change when they are signed.","kind":"comment","references":"1301ac856e3699cf3b51fdfc2b83022f18691710dffe26e5364dc72496b67513","summary":"Fixed in the test, not closed here: it now makes its database at 63 from MIGRATIONS[..63] and measures only the commit that takes the schema version to 64; it passes with a migration 65 appended","tags":["review","claxbot-surfaces","tests","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/tests/store_on_vfs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:54:58.327381Z","id":"4ba85069d02490332961b5ecf0915b030a3d676d063d2c7e61ac95d404aa2769","body":{"detail":"migration_64_rebuilds_bot_runs_within_its_cost_a_run_on_the_vfs opens a fresh store (every table at MIGRATIONS.len()), runs BOT_RUNS_AT_63 (DROP TABLE bot_runs, a copy of migration 50's table and indexes, migration 63's ALTER, PRAGMA user_version = 63) and opens again. The second open runs every migration after 63 on tables that are already at the latest shape. Shown at d75222028 by appending `\"CREATE TABLE zz_probe (a TEXT);\"` to MIGRATIONS and running `bazel test //crates/clax-worker:store_on_vfs`: the test panics at store_on_vfs.rs:71 with `MigrationFailed { at: 64, detail: \"table zz_probe already exists ...\" }`; the file's other two tests pass. The next migration that adds a table or a column therefore breaks this test, with a message about the store's open and not the fixture. The copy itself matches migrations 50 and 63 today (crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs:1554-1578, :2151) and those are landed, so it cannot drift; it is 28 lines the test does not need. Also: the test takes the largest commit of the whole open as migration 64's, so a later migration that writes more than 64 does would be measured under its name.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":250},"end":{"line":279},"content_hash":"b50e00d90abb6a077b4412f3b93d75005b416afda2676697d8fa827df3615562"},"suggested_fix":"Make the database at 63 as the_store_repairs_a_database_an_older_build_migrated_on_the_vfs makes one at 23 (store_on_vfs.rs:151): on the VFS connection, execute clax_store::migrations::MIGRATIONS[..63] joined with `;` and then `PRAGMA user_version = 63`, and delete BOT_RUNS_AT_63 and the first open_store. Tried at d75222028 with the zz_probe migration still appended: //crates/clax-worker:store_on_vfs PASSED.","summary":"The migration-64 VFS test fails as soon as a migration 65 exists: it makes its database at 63 by opening a fresh store at the latest version and swapping in a hand copy of bot_runs","supersedes":"1301ac856e3699cf3b51fdfc2b83022f18691710dffe26e5364dc72496b67513","tags":["review","claxbot-surfaces","tests","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
